  "description": "PAFHAJ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H100 Ce4 Fe4 N16 O28,C1 H4 O1. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Fe1A (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe2A (Fe) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.441-3.894 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.87-130.09°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C49H104Ce4Fe4N16O29. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 tea (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
